{
  "page": 20,
  "lines": [
    {
      "text": "NATH YIN CHOU",
      "bbox": [
        268.7359924316406,
        41.200374603271484,
        340.54058837890625,
        50.106937408447266
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "approach and Hashemi et al. (2024) is in using a learned multi-step predictor instead of learned",
      "bbox": [
        90.0,
        94.42467498779297,
        522.0001220703125,
        104.17741394042969
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Koopman dynamics to compute reachable sets. We note that the CP-NNV method suffers from",
      "bbox": [
        90.0,
        107.97368621826172,
        522.0003051757812,
        117.72642517089844
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "more conservative reachable sets, particularly in the angular velocity (p, q, r) and angle (ϕ, θ, ψ)",
      "bbox": [
        90.0,
        120.73724365234375,
        522.0000610351562,
        131.64634704589844
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "dimensions. We attribute this to the difficulty of computing reachable sets accurately with a learned",
      "bbox": [
        90.0,
        135.07171630859375,
        522.0001220703125,
        144.82444763183594
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "multi-step predictor over long horizons. Conversely, ScaRe-Kro maintains consistently tight bounds",
      "bbox": [
        90.0,
        148.6207275390625,
        522.0001831054688,
        158.3734588623047
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "across all 12 dimensions, demonstrating that the Koopman linearization effectively mitigates the",
      "bbox": [
        90.0,
        162.17071533203125,
        521.9999389648438,
        171.92344665527344
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "“wrapping effect” that causes over-approximation in standard neural network verification.",
      "bbox": [
        90.0,
        175.7197265625,
        481.538330078125,
        185.4724578857422
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
